{"resourceIdentifier":"2484","resourceName":"WM ENERGY BIOGAS PLANT","description":"WM Energy Biogas Plant project is a biogas-to-energy project that will generate renewable energy by capturing biogas from animal manure -via anaerobic digestion- and utilizing it to produce thermal and electric energy through biogas systems. It is implemented by WM ENERJİ SANAYİ VE TİCARET SANAYİ ANONİM ŞİRKETİ in Tavşanlı district, Kütahya province, in Turkey. \r\n\r\nFrom a socio-economic perspective, agricultural activities, along with animal husbandry, have historically been a main household income source for those living in Tavşanlı. However, whilst the number of stockbreeders and poultry farms has substantially increased for the last years in the region, cattle manure generated at farms, which is left to decay at and around farms in aerobic conditions, has become a major environmental, economic and legal problem for cattle breeders and poultry farmers, as well as for the local people living around farms.\r\n\r\nThe project whose main feedstock will be cattle and chicken manure generated at farms in Tavşanlı, provides an environmentally friendly solution to this manure management problem. \r\n\r\nIn the project’s detailed technical feasibility study, it is estimated that approximately 150 tons of cattle manure and 70 tons of chicken manure generated at animal farms will be collected daily through special sewage trucks equipped with close-tanks in order to prevent any odor and/or manure leakages and to be fed into the anaerobic digesters at the proposed biogas power plant. \r\n\r\nThe biogas generator system to be installed will be designed with a total power of 1.501 MWe/h. The annual feed-in electricity is estimated to be 12,968,640 KWh. Whilst heat generated at the plant is used at the facility to warm the digesters, the electricity generated is directly fed to the national grid. \r\n\r\nWhilst providing sustainable development benefits to the host communities and the host country, the project is expected to annually generate net GHG emission reductions of 56,463 tCO2eq/y.","location":{"latitude":39.587758,"longitude":29.407436},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-04-15","endExclusive":"2021-05-16","endInclusive":"2021-05-15"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2484"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Kütahya"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"38471"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AMS-I.D.,AMS-III.D."}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Bureau Veritas India Private Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"13/03/2026"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 03/09/2019 - 02/09/2026"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=51654&IDKEY=dq934lkmsad39asjdkfj90qlkalsdkngaf98ulkandDfdvDdfhs71230866","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS-Draft Project-Description-Template-v4.0 WM ENERGY BIOGAS PLANT, rev01 (ID2484), Listing Request 032821.pdf","uploadDate":"2021-03-28T13:37:11.257Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=51653&IDKEY=a0e98hfalksuf098fnsdalfkjfoijmn4309JLKJFjlaksjfla9a71229487","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"VCS-Listing-Representation-Multiple-Representors-v4.1